{"availability":"available","full":"Sorogate/sorogate","name":"sorogate","description":"Reusable access policies for Stellar, stored in a Soroban contract and evaluated the same way on-chain and in TypeScript. Early development, Testnet only.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":3,"created":"2026-10-06T17:42:48Z","updated":"2026-10-14T18:00:48Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sorogate.github.io/sorogate/","topics":["access-control","rust","smart-contracts","soroban","stellar","typescript"],"demo":"https://sorogate.github.io/sorogate/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:48:50.498Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:48:50.498Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:48:50.498Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:23.877Z","stars":0,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:28:17.559Z","stars":2,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-16T15:48:50.498Z","stars":2,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Reusable access policies for Stellar, stored in a Soroban contract and evaluated the same way from other contracts and from TypeScript.","Status: early development. Testnet only. Not audited. Not production. There is one public development deployment on Stellar Testnet, described in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md. It is not a production deployment, and Testnet is reset from time to time. The other Testnet runs in docs/evidence used throwaway deployments.","An access policy is a short list of conditions about an address: holds at least N of this token, holds at least N of this collection, the ledger time is inside this window. All conditions must hold. A contract (or an app) asks evaluate(policyid, address) and gets back a decision with the reason when it is a denial. Because the rules live in one place, an owner can change them without redeploying every contract that depends on them."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sorogate/sorogate/blob/main/README.md","finge